Package: erhai-kernel
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: erhai-device-support (= @VERSION@)
Description: OnePlus Pad 2 Pro (erhai) mainline boot triplet @KERNEL_RELEASE@
 The signed boot / init_boot / vendor_boot set this tablet's bootloader needs,
 built from the mainline kernel, the ABL-compatible device tree and the port's
 initramfs. Every image carries an AVB hash footer: vbmeta lists boot as a
 chain partition, so an image without one is malformed metadata that even an
 unlocked bootloader refuses.
 .
 Installing the package hands the set to erhai-switch-install-ubuntu-images,
 which puts it in the switcher's store, rotates the previous set to
 ubuntu.prev/ and -- when Ubuntu is the system occupying the slot -- rewrites
 the slot in place. Nothing reboots: the new kernel runs at the next boot.
 So a kernel update is an apt upgrade, and a kernel that does not boot is one
 `erhai-switch` away from the previous one.
